    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nRoselli is a truly exceptional and rare coastal residence, offering a once-in-a-generation opportunity to acquire a substantial family home in one of Wicklow's most sought-after locations. Extending to approximately 159.4 sq. metres this impressive property sits proudly on a magnificent one-acre site with the extraordinary benefit of direct private access onto the golden sands of Brittas Bay beach, a feature seldom found and highly prized.\nHaving remained within the same family for generations, the current owners have cherished Roselli for many years and have now made the decision to pass this remarkable home on to a new family who can enjoy its unique coastal setting and exceptional lifestyle. The property benefits from previously granted planning permission for extension and renovation works, with several years remaining on the permission should a purchaser wish to further enhance the home. While entirely comfortable and spacious as it stands, the option for future development presents an exciting opportunity.\nOriginally constructed in the 1940s, Roselli has been thoughtfully extended and carefully maintained over the years, creating a substantial and welcoming family residence that blends character, comfort, and practicality. The mature gardens surrounding the property are simply enchanting, featuring established trees, colourful planting, and expansive lawns that provide a wonderful sense of privacy and seclusion.\nSet well back from the road behind two entrance gates, one which is electric, the property enjoys an impressive approach and complete privacy. The generous front and rear gardens offer ample space for family life, outdoor entertaining, and recreation, while the direct access to Brittas Bay beach allows residents to enjoy morning walks, sea swims, and endless days by the shore.\nThe setting is further enhanced by its spectacular orientation. The sun rises beautifully over the rear of the property each morning, while the front garden enjoys breathtaking sunsets that must be seen to be fully appreciated. Combining space, privacy, direct beach access, and generations of family history, Roselli represents a truly rare opportunity to embrace one of Ireland's most desirable coastal lifestyles.\n\nUpon entering Roselli, you are immediately struck by the wonderful sense of light and space that flows throughout the home. Large windows frame the surrounding gardens and flood the interiors with natural light, creating an inviting and welcoming atmosphere.\nThe main living room is a particularly impressive space, featuring a striking stone-clad feature wall, warm timber flooring, and an attractive fireplace complete with a large wood-burning stove, creating the perfect focal point for family gatherings and cosy evenings.\nTo the right of the entrance hall is a practical boot room leading to a spacious home office. This versatile room could easily serve as an additional bedroom if required, making it ideal for modern family living. Beyond this are two bright and generously proportioned double bedrooms, one of which benefits from its own en-suite bathroom.\nTo the left of the living room, a third bedroom enjoys an abundance of natural light and attractive timber flooring, creating a comfortable and peaceful retreat. A family bathroom and well-appointed utility room are conveniently located nearby, providing excellent functionality for everyday living.\nThe heart of the home is the charming dual-aspect kitchen, which enjoys stunning views over both the front and rear gardens, with the rolling Wicklow countryside beyond. This spacious and welcoming room features tiled flooring, an extensive range of floor and eye-level units, integrated appliances, a breakfast bar, and a beautiful butcher's block countertop. French doors provide direct access to the patio and rear gardens, seamlessly connecting indoor and outdoor living.\nFrom the kitchen, you enter the impressive principal bedroom, a bright and tranquil space finished with timber flooring. Steps lead up to a superb walk-in wardrobe, providing ample storage and adding a touch of luxury to this private sanctuary. Together, these rooms create a home that is both practical and comfortable, perfectly suited to family life while taking full advantage of Roselli's spectacular coastal setting.\n\nSpecial Features\n• Exceptional coastal residence extending to approximately 220 sq.m.\n• Magnificent 1-acre landscaped site with mature trees and planting\n• Direct private access to Brittas Bay Beach, a truly rare and sought-after feature\n• Spacious detached family home, beautifully maintained throughout the years\n• Previously granted planning permission for extension and renovation, with time remaining on the permission\n• Stunning front and rear gardens with extensive lawn areas\n• Spectacular sunrise views to the rear and breathtaking sunsets to the front\n• Four generous bedrooms, including principal suite with walk-in wardrobe\n• Large home office with potential for use as an additional bedroom\n• Bright, dual-aspect kitchen overlooking the gardens and countryside beyond\n• Oil-fired central heating\n• Fibre broadband available\n• Private well water supply\n• Septic tank\n• Ample parking and extensive outdoor space\n• Conveniently located just minutes from Wicklow Town\n• Easy access to the M11 motorway, providing excellent connectivity to Dublin and beyond\n• Rare opportunity to acquire a family home that has been cherished by the same family for generations\n• Unrivalled coastal lifestyle with beach walks, swimming, water sports, and nature on your doorstep\n• Electric Car Charging point\nRoselli is a truly unique property where privacy, space, mature gardens, and direct beach access combine to create one of the finest family homes to come to the market in the Brittas Bay area in recent years.”"
      },
